%% Retry Pattern - Exponential Backoff with Jitter
%% Version: 1.0.0
%% Date: 2025-10-27
%% Description: Complete retry pattern implementation for payment processing and webhooks

graph TB
    subgraph "Retry Pattern Components"
        RetryHandler[Retry Handler<br/>Orchestrator]
        RetryPolicy[Retry Policy<br/>Configuration]
        BackoffStrategy[Backoff Strategy<br/>Exponential + Jitter]
        RetryQueue[Retry Queue<br/>Persistent Storage]
    end

    subgraph "Retry Policy Configuration"
        PolicyConfig["Retry Policy:<br/>---<br/>maxAttempts: 5<br/>initialDelay: 1000ms<br/>maxDelay: 60000ms<br/>backoffMultiplier: 2<br/>jitterFactor: 0.1<br/>retryableErrors: [timeout, 5xx]"]
    end

    subgraph "Retry States"
        InitialAttempt[Attempt 1<br/>Delay: 0ms<br/>Status: Pending]

        Retry1[Attempt 2<br/>Delay: 1000ms<br/>Status: Retrying]

        Retry2[Attempt 3<br/>Delay: 2000ms + jitter<br/>Status: Retrying]

        Retry3[Attempt 4<br/>Delay: 4000ms + jitter<br/>Status: Retrying]

        Retry4[Attempt 5<br/>Delay: 8000ms + jitter<br/>Status: Retrying]

        MaxRetries[Max Attempts<br/>Delay: 16000ms + jitter<br/>Status: Failed]
    end

    subgraph "Operation Execution"
        Operation[Protected Operation<br/>Payment/Webhook/API]
        SuccessHandler[Success Handler<br/>Complete Operation]
        ErrorHandler[Error Handler<br/>Categorize Error]
        DeadLetterQueue[Dead Letter Queue<br/>Failed Operations]
    end

    subgraph "Backoff Calculation"
        BackoffCalc["Backoff Formula:<br/>---<br/>delay = min(<br/>  initialDelay * (multiplier ^ attempt),<br/>  maxDelay<br/>) + random(0, delay * jitter)<br/><br/>Example:<br/>Attempt 1: 1000ms<br/>Attempt 2: 2000ms + 200ms jitter<br/>Attempt 3: 4000ms + 400ms jitter<br/>Attempt 4: 8000ms + 800ms jitter<br/>Attempt 5: 16000ms + 1600ms jitter"]
    end

    subgraph "Error Classification"
        ErrorTypes["Retryable Errors:<br/>---<br/>- Network timeout<br/>- Connection refused<br/>- 503 Service Unavailable<br/>- 504 Gateway Timeout<br/>- Temporary DB errors<br/><br/>Non-Retryable Errors:<br/>---<br/>- 400 Bad Request<br/>- 401 Unauthorized<br/>- 404 Not Found<br/>- Validation errors<br/>- Business logic errors"]
    end

    subgraph "Monitoring"
        RetryMetrics[Retry Metrics<br/>---<br/>Total Attempts<br/>Success Rate<br/>Avg Retry Count<br/>Failure Rate]
        AlertSystem[Alert System<br/>Max Retries Exceeded]
    end

    %% Initial Execution
    RetryHandler -->|1. Execute| Operation
    Operation -->|2a. Success| SuccessHandler
    SuccessHandler -->|3. Complete| RetryHandler

    Operation -->|2b. Error| ErrorHandler
    ErrorHandler -->|3. Classify| ErrorHandler

    %% Non-Retryable Error
    ErrorHandler -->|4a. Non-Retryable| DeadLetterQueue
    DeadLetterQueue -->|5. Alert| AlertSystem

    %% Retryable Error - Start Retry
    ErrorHandler -->|4b. Retryable| RetryHandler
    RetryHandler -->|5. Check Policy| RetryPolicy
    RetryPolicy -->|6. Within Limits| BackoffStrategy

    %% Retry Attempts
    BackoffStrategy -->|7. Calculate Delay| BackoffCalc
    BackoffCalc -->|8. Wait| RetryHandler
    RetryHandler -->|9. Queue Retry| RetryQueue

    RetryQueue -->|10. Attempt 2| Retry1
    Retry1 -->|11. Execute| Operation

    Operation -->|12. Still Failing| ErrorHandler
    ErrorHandler -->|13. Retryable| BackoffStrategy
    BackoffStrategy -->|14. Delay 2s| Retry2

    Retry2 -->|15. Execute| Operation
    Operation -->|16. Still Failing| ErrorHandler
    ErrorHandler -->|17. Retryable| BackoffStrategy
    BackoffStrategy -->|18. Delay 4s| Retry3

    Retry3 -->|19. Execute| Operation
    Operation -->|20. Still Failing| ErrorHandler
    ErrorHandler -->|21. Retryable| BackoffStrategy
    BackoffStrategy -->|22. Delay 8s| Retry4

    Retry4 -->|23. Execute| Operation
    Operation -->|24. Still Failing| ErrorHandler
    ErrorHandler -->|25. Retryable| BackoffStrategy
    BackoffStrategy -->|26. Delay 16s| MaxRetries

    %% Max Retries Exceeded
    MaxRetries -->|27. Execute Final| Operation
    Operation -->|28. Final Failure| ErrorHandler
    ErrorHandler -->|29. Max Attempts| DeadLetterQueue
    DeadLetterQueue -->|30. Alert| AlertSystem

    %% Monitoring
    RetryHandler -.Metrics.-> RetryMetrics
    BackoffStrategy -.Metrics.-> RetryMetrics
    ErrorHandler -.Metrics.-> RetryMetrics

    %% Configuration
    PolicyConfig -.Configure.-> RetryPolicy
    ErrorTypes -.Configure.-> ErrorHandler

    %% Key Characteristics
    Note1["Retry Pattern Benefits:<br/>✓ Transient fault tolerance<br/>✓ Network resilience<br/>✓ Improved reliability<br/>✓ Automatic recovery<br/>✓ Graceful degradation"]

    Note2["Exponential Backoff:<br/>- Prevents thundering herd<br/>- Reduces server load<br/>- Allows time for recovery<br/>- Jitter prevents collision<br/>- Configurable limits"]

    Note3["Use Cases:<br/>- Payment processing<br/>- Webhook delivery<br/>- External API calls<br/>- Database operations<br/>- NOSTR relay publishing<br/>- Email sending"]

    Note4["Best Practices:<br/>1. Set max retry limits<br/>2. Use exponential backoff<br/>3. Add jitter randomization<br/>4. Classify error types<br/>5. Monitor retry metrics<br/>6. Alert on failures<br/>7. Use idempotency keys"]

